<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_SweetlineTree — TREE_GRAPHICS_OWNERSHIP_1, our own art at our own scale.
    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/arid_shrubland.md §4 "The sweetline trees":
    "Huge, ancient, powerful things (owner's ruling — never small trees). Each
    grows only on the optimum, so each is a living surveyor's mark, visible for
    a day's walk; roads follow them and every one has a name. Giants rub
    against them, so the bark snags shed giant-wool."

    ParentName="TreeBase" (Defs/Core/ThingDefs_Plants/Plants_Bases.xml) rather
    than DeciduousTreeBase — this is a fixed-sun tidally-locked world with no
    day/night or season cycle (arid_shrubland.md §6 rule 3), so the fall-colour
    shader parameters DeciduousTreeBase carries do not apply.

    Scale: plant.visualSizeRange caps at 10.0 — owner's ruling on
    ASHKARR_FLORA_SWEETLINE_ART_UNWIRED_1 ("Make that sweetline tree ten cells
    wide"), a canopy 10 tiles wide at full growth, up from the earlier 6.5 cap
    (same 5.0:6.5 min:max spread ratio carried forward: 7.7~10.0). Still well
    above vanilla's biggest common tree (Plant_TreePine, 3.0~6.0 under the
    BetterTrees Djeeshka template referenced below) and matching the "huge,
    ancient" ruling without inventing a multi-tile footprint. A true
    monumental multi-cell object (giants rubbing against it, named road anchor,
    hand-placed one-per-sweetline rather than random wildPlants scatter) is
    still Owed — see items/TREE_GRAPHICS_OWNERSHIP_1.md — this def only closes
    the ART/SCALE-OWNERSHIP half of the ticket.

    shadowData is UNCHANGED from the 6.5-cap version, deliberately, not
    overlooked: checked vanilla Core (Plants_Bases.xml TreeBase 1.5~2.0 ->
    volume 0.2/0.35/0.13; Plant_TreePine 1.5~3.0, a 50% larger visualSizeRange
    -> volume 0.15/0.3/0.15, SMALLER than TreeBase's) — the shadow ellipsoid
    tracks the trunk's ground footprint, not the canopy's visual size, and
    vanilla shows no scaling relationship between the two at all. Scaling it
    by the same 10/6.5 factor as the canopy would be exactly the "ceiling
    fields break when doubled" trap (CLAUDE.md).

    Fourteen art variants land with this change (all candidates recovered in
    _artsrc/sweetline_orphans_2026-09-06/, owner: "I absolutely love ALL of
    them. Please accept them all as alternative art that it rotates between")
    — RUT_SweetlineTreeA.png..N.png, 1280x1280 (10 cells x 128 px/cell, same
    literal formula the README used for the old 768x768/6.0-cell canvas).
    Graphic_Random groups them by the filename prefix before any underscore,
    so bare letter suffixes (no "_" before the letter) is load-bearing, not
    style. Each tree was cropped to its own visible-canopy bounding box then
    fit (aspect preserved) into the SAME target frame on the shared canvas —
    normalizing away the source renders' wildly different padding so the
    variety reads as fourteen different ancient trees, not fourteen different
    scales of the same tree.

    Flammability 0.1 (down from TreeBase's 0.8): arid_shrubland.md §6 rule 9,
    "No flammable living flora" — a hard ban, not a judgment call.

    growDays/harvestWork raised well past TreeBase's defaults as flavour for
    "ancient" and "huge" respectively; not a balance pass. mustBeWildToSow
    stays true (inherited) — the tree can never be planted by a colonist,
    matching "each grows only on the optimum."
  -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="TreeBase">
    <defName>RUT_SweetlineTree</defName>
    <label>sweetline tree</label>
    <description>A single ancient giant, centuries old, growing only where the moisture-light trade balances exactly. Its trunk is scarred smooth in patches where the biome's giants have rubbed against it for longer than any settlement nearby has stood; the bark sheds their snagged wool in long silver hanks. Every sweetline tree has a name, and the roads of the shrubland are laid tree to tree along the line they mark.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RUT_SweetlineTree</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.45, 0.6, 0.32)</volume>
        <offset>(0,0,-0.46)</offset>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>650</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.1</Flammability>
      <Mass>900</Mass>
      <BeautyOutdoors>10</BeautyOutdoors>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <visualSizeRange>7.7~10.0</visualSizeRange>
      <growDays>240</growDays>
      <harvestWork>4200</harvestWork>
      <harvestYield>160</harvestYield>
      <wildClusterRadius>0</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>0.05</wildClusterWeight>
      <wildOrder>4</wildOrder>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
